# What this port was written against.
#
# Nothing here is a mirror, so there is no tree to diff and no patch to
# reapply. These are the references the algorithms were ported from and the
# corpora generated by, recorded so that a later reader can check a formula
# against the same source this one used.

s2geometry
  https://github.com/google/s2geometry
  tag        v0.14.0
  license    Apache-2.0
  role       the reference implementation. Every algorithm, constant and error
             bound in the port comes from here: the quadratic projection and
             its metrics, the Hilbert lookup tables, the escalating orientation
             predicate and its symbolic perturbation, the region coverer's
             refinement heuristic, and the cap and rectangle bounds.

             Two files from it are also read by tools/: s2loop_test.cc and
             s2polygon_test.cc, whose fixtures and relation tables become
             tests/LoopRelationCorpus.roc and tests/PolygonCorpus.roc. Those are
             upstream's own answers for which shape contains which, degenerate
             cases included. Neither file is bundled.

             tests/CoverCorpus.roc and the expected coverings in
             src/S2RegionCoverer.roc come from running upstream's C++
             S2RegionCoverer at this tag. tools/cover_oracle.cc is the driver,
             linked against s2geometry v0.14.0 and abseil-cpp 20250814.1, and
             tools/generate_corpus.py runs it. The corpus was generated with
             libc++, whose priority queue decides the order of candidates
             with equal priority.

s2sphere
  https://github.com/sidewalklabs/s2sphere
  revision   master, 2026-08-30
  license    MIT
  role       an independent Python port of the same library, used only to
             generate the golden corpora in tests/ other than CoverCorpus.
             Running it is what makes the corpora a cross-check rather than a
             snapshot of this port's own output. Its region coverer is the
             older algorithm, so the cover corpus comes from upstream instead.
             Not bundled, and not needed to build or test.

Shewchuk, Jonathan Richard
  "Adaptive Precision Floating-Point Arithmetic and Fast Robust Geometric
  Predicates", Discrete & Computational Geometry 18(3), 1997
  role       the expansion arithmetic in S2Exact.

Edelsbrunner, Herbert and Ernst Peter Muecke
  "Simulation of Simplicity: A Technique to Cope with Degenerate Cases in
  Geometric Algorithms", ACM Transactions on Graphics 9(1), 1990
  role       the symbolic perturbation that gives exactly collinear points a
             consistent orientation.
